---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What voicegateway.dev collects, why, and how to have it removed. A waitlist email and page analytics; never your call audio.">
  <Prose
    title="Privacy"
    lead="The short version: if you join the waitlist we keep your email to tell you when a hosted version ships, and we count page visits. We do not sell either, and we never touch your call audio."
  >
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your waitlist email.</strong> When you submit the form, we store the address, the time, and which form it came from.</li>
      <li><strong>Page analytics.</strong> PostHog records page views and clicks on this site, to tell us which pages are useful.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>There is no account, login or payment on this site.</p>

    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>The email is only for telling you when a hosted VoiceGateway is available. The analytics are only for improving this site.</p>

    <h2>Where it is stored, and who sees it</h2>
    <p>
      Waitlist emails are stored in a Postgres database hosted by Neon, and only the VoiceGateway team can read them.
      Analytics go to PostHog. We do not sell, rent or share your email, and we do not use it for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Your call audio</h2>
    <p>
      VoiceGateway records per-request cost and latency, not conversations. It never stores or processes the live
      audio of your agents, and when you self-host it, that telemetry stays on your own infrastructure.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      To see or delete what we hold about you, email <a href="mailto:mahi@mahimai.ca">mahi@mahimai.ca</a> and we will
      remove your waitlist entry promptly.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">Last updated: September 2026</p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
